(6112912, 899616, 69668, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> this probably falls under the category of the discussion that has taken place as of late. i imagine you got exactly the look you were going for, and exactly the contrast as well. its not often a nude gets a high placing in a non nude challenge. nice work. however in my opinion some art is better appreciated on a wall in a gallery than in a challenge such as this.<br/> <br/>p.s. i keep meaning to tell you this reminds me of those famous nude shots of Marylin Monroe shortly before she died. Again, lovely work Jen. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks Jason for the kind words.  I actually was going for a Marilyn Monroe type image (I put this image in the vintage gallery as well as nude).....so I am glad that it came across that way.</td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: this probably falls under the category of the discussion that has taken place as of late. i imagine you got exactly the look you were going for, and exactly the contrast as well. its not often a nude gets a high placing in a non nude challenge. nice work. however in my opinion some art is better appreciated on a wall in a gallery than in a challenge such as this. p.s. i keep meaning to tell you this reminds me of those famous nude shots of Marylin Monroe shortly before she died. Again, lovely work Jen.   Thanks Jason for the kind words.  I actually was going for a Marilyn Monroe type image (I put this image in the vintage gallery as well as nude).....so I am glad that it came across that way.', '2010-08-02 02:07:52.000000', NULL, 0),
